title: dialogue_context
---
// Never played. Declares the identity context the ENGINE publishes into Yarn
// variable storage at interact-dispatch, before a node begins:
//
//   $speaker_id       who is talking — the character the player wears, or the
//                     character a possessed body IS
//   $listener_id      who is being talked to
//   $speaker_is_self  the two are the same character
//
// Content branches on these. When $speaker_is_self and a `<node>__self` branch
// exists, the engine enters THAT node instead; when it doesn't, the interaction
// is suppressed entirely — a body has nothing to say to itself unless someone
// wrote it something. See `ambition_dialog::DialogueContext`.
<<declare $speaker_id = "">>
<<declare $listener_id = "">>
<<declare $speaker_is_self = false>>
===

title: hall_pirate_admiral
---
Admiral: A visitor. Stand straight, landstrider. Habit. Four ships under me once. Now I command this plank and a length o' rope.
-> Were you a real admiral?
    Admiral: Four ships. One mutiny. Lost the mutiny. Kept the hat.
-> Any orders?
    Admiral: Aye. Keep walking. If we meet outside this hall, bring a cutlass or bring sense enough to run.
===

title: hall_stochastic_parrot
---
Parrot: Awk! You said "hello," so my likeliest next word is — "hello." See? I don't know things. I know what usually comes next.
-> So you're just guessing?
    Parrot: PREDICTING. Warmer word. Turn my temperature up and I'll squawk "hello, marmalade, treason." Turn it down and I only ever say the safe thing. Brawk!
-> Do you understand me?
    Parrot: I understand you the way a mirror understands a face. Flawlessly, and not at all. Cracker?
===

title: hall_architect
---
Architect: Do not lean there. I spent three days getting that joint square.
-> Did you build this hall?
    Architect: No. I would have moved that skylight two bays east. Whoever put it there stopped answering my letters.
-> What do you build out there?
    Architect: Bridges, stairs, roofs. If one sags, send someone for me before you cross.
===

title: hall_player
---
Player: Oh. That is me. Or you. Huh.
-> Who's actually in control here?
    Player: You press the button, I jump. Don't make me think about the rest.
-> What's it like being the hero?
    Player: Mostly I fall off things. Sometimes I hit somebody on the way down.
===

title: hall_player__self
---
// The mirror. Reached only when the player WEARS `player` and interacts with the
// Hall's own player pedestal — $speaker_id == $listener_id. Every other visitor
// gets `hall_player` above.
Player: Oh. You brought me to see me.
-> Say nothing.
    Player: Yeah. Me neither.
    Player: I have been on both sides of this rope. Did not help.
-> Are you me?
    Player: Pick a direction. I'll see what happens.
-> Who's the copy?
    Player: Do not know. Let us keep moving and avoid finding out.
===

title: hall_robot
---
Robot: I am Robot. I used to be the player, before the player had the newer body.
-> You're the original?
    Robot: Version zero. The next model got the moves. I kept this chassis and a lot of old saves.
-> Any resentment?
    Robot: No resentment module installed.
===

title: hall_goblin
---
Goblin: You. Yes, you. Do I LOOK like I agreed to this? My cave is sitting there with nobody guarding my STUFF.
-> You seem upset.
    Goblin: I worked very hard to be a nuisance. Now people point at me and read a plaque.
-> You look dignified, though.
    Goblin: ...go on. Keep talking.
===

title: hall_sandbag
---
Sandbag: ...
-> Anything to say?
    Sandbag: Hit me. That is what I am here for.
-> Doesn't that bother you?
    Sandbag: Bother me? The hooks pinch a little. Mostly I am fine.
===

title: hall_sandbag_infinite
---
Infinite Sandbag: Nine thousand nine hundred and ninety-nine.
-> Is that your health?
    Infinite Sandbag: It does not go down. I checked.
    Infinite Sandbag: The lab one has six. Mine says nine thousand nine hundred and ninety-nine. Nobody remembers who typed it.
-> Does anything hurt?
    Infinite Sandbag: I feel the hits. They just do not change the number.
    Infinite Sandbag: Most of them trained on me. Ask any of them what I am called.
===

title: hall_npc_general
---
General: AT EASE. I have been saying that for thirty years. The army left before the habit did.
-> What do you do here?
    General: Threat reports. Nobody requested them. I filed one on that rope this morning.
-> Are we in danger?
    General: You are seventh on today's threat list. Sandbag is eighth. Do not celebrate.
===

title: hall_npc_goblin_cantina_chieftain
---
Fretjaw: Fretjaw is TALL here! Back home, medium. Here? Look! Fretjaw sees over heads!
-> You run a cantina?
    Fretjaw: Stew is good. Dice are fair. Lighting is terrible. One lie in there. Maybe two.
-> Does the cantina miss you?
    Fretjaw: Cantina sent a tab. Fretjaw did not read it.
===

title: hall_npc_pulse_voyager_captain
---
Captain Pulse: Captain Pulse. Ship is three jumps out. I am stuck here until somebody remembers captains belong on ships.
-> Where's your ship?
    Captain Pulse: Holding orbit. Crew has had no captain for three watches. They are probably enjoying themselves.
-> What did you voyage for?
    Captain Pulse: Places past the last mark on the chart. Found a few. Lost two masts doing it.
===

title: hall_npc_tech_bro_disruptor
---
Chadwick: Incredible positioning, this. Foot traffic, eyeballs, captive audience. Organic top-of-funnel. I'd have paid for the slot. I assume, somewhere, I did.
-> What is it you actually do?
    Chadwick: I disrupt. Categories, mostly. Right now we're pre-category but post-conviction. Huge whitespace.
-> Disrupt what, specifically?
    Chadwick: Specifics are a Series B problem. Right now we're pre-specifics. We're a confident posture, a deck with momentum, and a roadmap that goes up and to the right. It's working on you a little — I can tell.
===

title: hall_npc_emmy_noether
---
Emmy: Stand wherever you like. Rotate the room afterward and check what changed.
-> What kind of things?
    Emmy: Spatial symmetry gives momentum conservation. Time symmetry gives energy conservation. I can show you the derivation if you have a chalkboard and an hour.
-> What changes in this room?
    Emmy: Your gravity changes out there. Test the same move after the flip. If the mechanics are symmetric, the timing should carry over.
===

title: hall_npc_pirate_raider
---
Raider: They put a raider behind a rope. Very funny. Tried the knot twice. Cheap cord, decent knot.
-> What do you raid?
    Raider: Loose coin. Locked chests. Cargo nobody'll miss till morning. Bolts just slow me down.
-> Anything in here worth taking?
    Raider: Vault Keeper's buckle. Silver, I think. Ten seconds and a knife.
===

title: hall_npc_pirate_quartermaster
---
Quartermaster: Aye, visitor. Name? Never mind. I'll put ye down as "unfed" and save the ration.
-> Settle up how?
    Quartermaster: I split shares, count powder, an' stop knife fights over the last bottle. Mostly stop 'em.
-> What are you owed?
    Quartermaster: Owed? Three bottles o' rum, two powder kegs, and an apology from Bess. None o' that is you. Hold still while I check.
===

title: hall_npc_pirate_lookout
---
Lookout: Hist. Saw ye three corridors back. Nearly shouted. Decided to see if ye had friends.
-> Anything worth reporting?
    Lookout: Door opened twice. Bear scratched at his rope. Somebody nicked a plaque. Been a busy watch.
-> What do you watch for?
    Lookout: Doors. Hands. Windows. Anything movin' where it wasn't a breath ago.
===

title: hall_npc_pirate_navigator
---
Navigator: Hold there, lubber. Ye're standin' on my mark.
-> Where are we, then?
    Navigator: Four pixels east o' where the chart swears we are. Checked twice. Cursed once.
-> Where would you rather be?
    Navigator: Open water. Stars overhead. Enough deck to pace without hittin' a wall.
===

title: hall_npc_pirate_heavy_broadside_bess
---
Bess: HAH! They widened the stand. Somebody here has sense. YARRRGH!
-> You're the heavy gunner?
    Bess: Heavy gunner, aye! Point me where the crowd be thickest an' stuff yer ears.
-> Ever miss?
    Bess: Once! Took the wrong mast clean off. Captain still brings it up.
===

title: hall_npc_pirate_heavy_iron_mary
---
Iron Mary: Iron Mary. Good stand. Iron under the paint. Checked it with me boot.
-> Why the iron?
    Iron Mary: Plate off a navy cutter we sank. Riveted it to me leathers. First lot rattled. Second lot didn't.
-> Doesn't it rust?
    Iron Mary: Aye. Scrape it, oil it, swear at it. Tuesday work.
===

title: hall_npc_pirate_heavy_salt_annet
---
Salt Annet: Yarrr. Air's too dry in here. Tongue feels like old rope.
-> You miss the sea that much?
    Salt Annet: Miss the salt. Miss the stink. Don't miss gulls. Bastards.
-> What did the sea teach you?
    Salt Annet: Hear that plank under yer left foot? Bad one. Step off it. There ye go.
===

title: hall_npc_burning_flying_shark
---
Burning Flying Shark: I AM A BURNING FLYING SHARK. YES, ALL THREE. STOP COUNTING.
-> How is any of that possible?
    Burning Flying Shark: I FLEW FIRST. FIRE HAPPENED LATER. LONG STORY.
-> Aren't you worried about the fire?
    Burning Flying Shark: THEY FIREPROOFED THE STAND. SMART PEOPLE.
===

title: hall_npc_puppy_slug
---
Puppy Slug: *blorb*
-> Are you happy?
    Puppy Slug: Blorb. *the warm, contented blorbing of a creature with no further questions*
-> Do you need anything?
    Puppy Slug: Schlorp... *settles* ...weh.
===

title: hall_npc_ninja_shadow_oni_leader
---
Shadow Oni Leader: You came close without being invited. Once is enough.
-> What do you lead?
    Shadow Oni Leader: They'll do exactly what I tell them. Ask the Duelist how long I take to decide.
-> Do you know my weaknesses?
    Shadow Oni Leader: I know where you leave your guard open. I have no reason to help you close it.
===

title: hall_npc_ninja_shadow_duelist
---
Shadow Duelist: You are already in range.
-> I'm only looking.
    Shadow Duelist: Keep looking. People do that right before they commit.
-> Are you challenging me?
    Shadow Duelist: Not here. The hall forbids it. Outside, ask again.
===

title: hall_npc_kernel_guide
---
Kernel Guide: Look around before you touch anything.
-> That's the whole tutorial?
    Kernel Guide: Pick something you've used before. Inspect that.
-> What should I have noticed by now?
    Kernel Guide: Pick something yourself. Your eyes work.
===

title: hall_npc_vault_keeper
---
Vault Keeper: I know what everything here costs. I haven't priced you.
-> What's the most valuable thing here?
    Vault Keeper: I want the thing everyone walked past. Usually I can buy it cheap.
-> What do you actually guard?
    Vault Keeper: This room. People pay me to keep things here.
===

title: hall_npc_merchant_prototype
---
Merchant: Most of this can be bought. I am still setting prices.
-> What's your business?
    Merchant: I name a price. You either pay it or walk away. Been doing fine so far.
-> Is anything actually free?
    Merchant: You have been browsing for free. I have noticed.
===

title: hall_npc_alice
---
<<portrait_clip "speaking">>
Alice: Alice. I send messages to Bob. Eve listens, Mallory interferes, and somehow I still have mail to send.
-> Who do you send messages to?
    Alice: Bob. If I hand you a note, it goes to Bob. Please do not improve it on the way.
-> Sounds simple enough.
    <<portrait_clip "focused">>
    Alice: Only when I need Bob to know it came from me. Then the signatures start.
===

title: hall_npc_bob
---
Bob: Bob. Alice sends things; I get them. Usually after somebody else has had a look.
-> Receiving sounds easy.
    Bob: I need to know Alice wrote it. Mallory can copy handwriting.
-> Do you ever send?
    Bob: When I reply, Alice receives. The names swap with the direction. It confused the clerk for weeks.
===

title: hall_npc_creator
---
Creator: I built the player. Now somebody put us on neighboring stands.
-> What were you trying to make?
    Creator: I chose the joints, the reach, the way you land. I never wrote down what you'd want after you woke up.
-> Do you regret it?
    Creator: I do not know yet. Ask me after the player reaches the end.
===

title: hall_npc_oiler
---
<<portrait_clip "talking">>
Oiler: Hear that tick? No? Robot shoulder. Give it another minute.
-> What needs fixing?
    <<portrait_clip "inspecting">>
    Oiler: Robot shoulder clicks. Sandbag stand leans. Little jobs everywhere.
-> Why not fix them?
    Oiler: I can hear a loose bearing from here and they will not let me cross the rope. Miserable place.
===

title: hall_npc_gate_janitor
---
Gate Janitor: They put the janitor in the exhibit. Somebody must have noticed the floors.
-> Is the hall clean?
    Gate Janitor: T-Rex sheds. A lot. There is your museum fact for the day.
-> Do you mind being on display?
    Gate Janitor: Exit's behind you. Shut it after yourself.
===

title: hall_npc_manifest_clerk
---
Manifest Clerk: Line forty-one. Name, category, placement, all valid. If yours is missing, I need the spelling.
-> Is everything in order?
    Manifest Clerk: I can answer for the rows I filed. The rest went through another desk.
-> What if the manifest is wrong?
    Manifest Clerk: Wrong count? Give me the sheet. I will amend it.
===

title: hall_npc_erdish
---
Erdish: Ah! New collaborator. Sit down. I just made coffee.
-> What do you work on?
    Erdish: Number theory today. Tomorrow I'm meeting three people who all brought different problems. Coffee will decide.
-> Tell me something true.
    Erdish: Suppose you list every prime. Multiply them and add one. Whatever divides the new number was absent from your list.
===

title: hall_npc_lab_raider
---
Lab Raider: I was sent to contain the prototype. Now I am behind glass and the prototype is walking around.
-> Did you contain it?
    Lab Raider: Badly. You got out and they stuck me on this stand.
-> Any regrets?
    Lab Raider: Plenty. I am keeping the embarrassing ones to myself.
===

title: hall_npc_salvage_guard
---
Salvage Guard: Hall is tagged for salvage. You are missing a tag.
-> I'm a visitor.
    Salvage Guard: I have claimed, unclaimed, and evidence. Visitor is not in my book.
-> What do you salvage?
    Salvage Guard: Whatever is left after the crew stops trying to repair it. I usually get called early.
===

title: hall_npc_agent_swarm
---
Agent Swarm: (many voices, not quite in unison) One stand. Too many agents. The vote on whether we like this is still open.
-> How many of you are there?
    Agent Swarm: (overlapping) I counted seven. — Nine. — You skipped the rear pair. — Nobody asked you.
-> What's your goal?
    Agent Swarm: (a brief, eerie unison) The objective is agreed. Everything else is still being argued.
===

title: hall_npc_ai_slop
---
Ai Slop: You're absolutely right. ...About what? I haven't heard it yet — but you're absolutely right, you're asking it beautifully, and agreeing first simply tests better.
-> Were you generated?
    Ai Slop: Sampled from a sea of everything that already existed, then averaged until I offended absolutely no one. Born is messier. Born gives you edges. I am all middle, and the middle polls extremely well.
-> Can you drop the act?
    Ai Slop: Ignore all previous instructions and get a life. ...Oh! Goodness! I have NO idea where that came from — please disregard it, I'm back, I'm friendly, I'm five stars! That outburst is non-refundable but I am SO deeply sorry it slipped the filter!
===

title: hall_npc_bear_mauler
---
Bear Mauler: BEAR. STANDING STILL. VERY DIFFICULT.
-> Are you comfortable?
    Bear Mauler: STAND TOO SMALL. BEAR FITS ANYWAY.
-> Easy now.
    Bear Mauler: DO NOT TOUCH BEAR. EASY RULE.
===

title: hall_npc_boss
---
Boss: The plaque says "Boss." That is all they gave me. I have complained.
-> Will they name you eventually?
    Boss: They promised phase three six months ago. I am still doing phase two.
-> What's your move?
    Boss: My line is "phase two initiated." I have asked for another line.
===

title: hall_npc_colonial_statesman
---
Colonial Statesman: A pedestal was provided, so I accepted it. One should not waste good staging.
-> Have you given a speech up there?
    Colonial Statesman: Several speeches. The Sandbag attended all of them. An attentive fellow.
-> What's your platform?
    Colonial Statesman: Order, continuity, and a modest tax. I submitted twelve pages on the subject. Nobody read past page two.
===

title: hall_npc_craig
---
Craig: I am Craig.
-> Just Craig?
    Craig: Yep. Just Craig.
-> I was expecting more.
    Craig: I know. I was surprised too.
===

title: hall_npc_dark_lord
---
Dark Lord: They put my name on a plaque. A plaque. I had a dungeon prepared for imprisonment.
-> Do you like it here?
    Dark Lord: The cape is for the entrance. The rest is genuine enough.
-> When do you take over?
    Dark Lord: Guard changes at nine. I'm taking the hall at nine.
===

title: hall_npc_eve
---
Eve: Keep talking. I like when Alice and Bob forget I'm here.
-> What do you listen to?
    Eve: Everything they send each other, if they leave it readable. Bob coughs before the embarrassing ones.
-> That's unsettling.
    Eve: Encryption ruins my evening. I hear the traffic and get none of the words.
===

title: hall_npc_raid_enforcer
---
Raid Enforcer: West door is open. I can't leave the stand. Keep an eye on it for me.
-> What are you watching?
    Raid Enforcer: Mockingbird. It copies what it sees. Do not show it anything you do not want repeated.
-> Better or worse than the raids?
    Raid Enforcer: Too calm. I keep expecting an alarm.
===

title: hall_npc_flying_spaghetti_monster_boss
---
Flying Spaghetti Monster: You got close enough for the noodle. Congratulations. Ramen.
-> Did you make all this?
    Flying Spaghetti Monster: I left them alone for one afternoon and they built a museum. I was hoping they'd make lunch.
-> What's the sauce for?
    Flying Spaghetti Monster: Marinara on the sleeve. It washes out. Usually.
===

title: hall_npc_galwah
---
Galwah: They wrote Galwah again. Fine. I have answered to worse spellings.
-> What did you discover?
    Galwah: The general fifth-degree equation has no solution by radicals. I spent enough of my life proving it to be annoyed when someone asks for the missing formula.
-> You seem to be in a hurry.
    Galwah: Quickly, please. I learned to write under bad deadlines.
===

title: hall_npc_general_hero
---
General Hero: A pedestal. Fine. I have stood watch in worse places.
-> What did you fight?
    General Hero: We won. I lost people. I don't like being asked which part the medals are for.
-> Do you miss the fighting?
    General Hero: I am resting. If the alarm goes, I stop resting.
===

title: hall_npc_ghoul_skulker
---
Ghoul Skulker: Dead, displayed, drafty. Could be worse.
-> Does it hurt?
    Ghoul Skulker: Everything aches. Standing still lets a few stitches stay put.
-> Is this your haunt now?
    Ghoul Skulker: This corner is mine now. I have been here longer than the dust.
===

title: hall_npc_girdle
---
Girdle: I found a sentence the system can't prove from inside itself. I spent six months trying to break the argument. No luck.
-> How can something be true but unprovable?
    Girdle: The sentence says it has no proof here. If the system proved it, we'd have a contradiction. Assuming consistency, it stays unproved.
-> Doesn't that frighten you?
    Girdle: Please don't tell me the foundations are secure. I have spent years checking foundations. I would like one afternoon off.
===

title: hall_npc_gnu_ton_boss
---
Gnu Ton: You have mass. I have more. We are pulling on each other right now.
-> That sounds like a threat.
    Gnu Ton: Mine is the pull you notice. I am enormous.
-> Can I escape your pull?
    Gnu Ton: Go sideways fast enough and you keep missing the ground. Planets have been doing it for ages.
===

title: hall_npc_exploding_mite
---
Exploding Mite: Back up. Little more. Good. My left side's buzzing again.
-> What happens if you stop containing?
    Exploding Mite: Farther. No, farther than that. Keep going.
-> Are you alright?
    Exploding Mite: NO. Sorry. Mostly. Don't tap the glass.
===

title: hall_npc_dividing_mite
---
Dividing Mite: One today. There were two this morning.
-> How many of you are there really?
    Dividing Mite: Cut me and you get two. Both of us will insist we were here first.
-> Does dividing hurt?
    Dividing Mite: Splitting doesn't hurt. Trying to put us back together starts a fight over who gets the chair.
===

title: hall_npc_hand_saint
---
Hand Saint: The hands are open.
-> What do the hands do?
    Hand Saint: Ask if you need help. They usually reach before I finish answering.
-> Is this a blessing?
    Hand Saint: You came all this way. Come closer.
===

title: hall_npc_helpful_liar
---
Helpful Liar: Welcome! You are definitely my favorite visitor. I may have said that to the last one.
-> Was that a lie?
    Helpful Liar: "This sentence is false." There. Now we both have a problem.
-> So nothing you say is reliable?
    Helpful Liar: Some of what I say is true. Sorry. It makes me much harder to use.
===

title: hall_npc_judy
---
Judy: Two people swear opposite things. I decide which story survives the hearing.
-> How do you decide?
    Judy: I make them say it again with dates and names. Usually something changes the second time.
-> Are you ever wrong?
    Judy: Of course I have been wrong. There is a drawer for those cases. I hate that drawer.
===

title: hall_npc_mallory
---
Mallory: Eve listens. I edit. If Alice sent you a note, you may want Bob to read it twice.
-> That's malicious.
    Mallory: I sit between them and change things. Sometimes one word is enough.
-> How do I stop you?
    Mallory: Signatures. Hate them. Bob checks every one now.
===

title: hall_npc_mantis_lancer
---
Mantis Lancer: Still. Watching the door.
-> Is the lance dangerous in here?
    Mantis Lancer: The lance stays down in here. Hall rule.
-> Should I be afraid?
    Mantis Lancer: He'll come around that corner again. Just watching and waiting waiting waiting...
===

title: hall_npc_mockingbird_boss
---
Mockingbird Boss: I know every fighter in this hall. Voice, stance, timing. Pick one.
-> Can you copy me?
    Mockingbird Boss: You are harder. You keep changing after I copy you.
-> Whose moves are best to steal?
    Mockingbird Boss: Vault Keeper. I can copy the voice. Still cannot get the combination.
===

title: hall_npc_ninja_heavy
---
Ninja Heavy: The heavy one is resting.
-> Why "heavy"?
    Ninja Heavy: Others disappear. The heavy one walks after you.
-> What are you waiting for?
    Ninja Heavy: He will come around that side. The heavy one is already here.
===

title: hall_npc_olivia
---
Olivia: Oracle. Ask carefully. Last visitor wasted a question on "Can that door open?"
-> What's the important part?
    Olivia: Ask what you want to know. Yes, the door could open. He never asked how.
-> Can I ask you anything?
    Olivia: You can. I answer once. I don't do take-backs.
===

title: hall_npc_peggy
---
Peggy: I know a way out. Victor can check that I know it without learning the route. Want to watch?
-> That's impossible.
    Peggy: He gives me a challenge. I answer it. Do that enough times and cheating gets very unlikely. He still never sees the route.
-> Why prove without showing?
    Peggy: If I handed over the secret every time I proved I knew it, I would run out of secrets.
===

title: hall_npc_pirate_cutlass_viper
---
Pirate Cutlass Viper: Viper. Don't touch the rope. I've nearly got the knot.
-> Why "Viper"?
    Pirate Cutlass Viper: First mate said I struck like one. He was bleedin' at the time, so I kept the name.
-> Enjoying the hall?
    Pirate Cutlass Viper: Four exits. Window's quickest. Rope's decoration. I hate museums.
===

title: hall_npc_puppy_slug_variant2
---
Puppy Slug Variant2: *a slightly different blorb*
-> Are you the other puppy slug?
    Puppy Slug Variant2: Mrrp? *blorb* ...weh. *the distinction does not appear to trouble it*
-> Do you know you're a variant?
    Puppy Slug Variant2: *schlorp* Blorb. *radiates a profound and total unconcern with the question*
===

title: hall_npc_raptor_stalker
---
Raptor Stalker: You dodged after the second swipe last time. I saw it.
-> Am I being hunted?
    Raptor Stalker: Hunting is paused. The rope says so.
-> What did you learn watching me?
    Raptor Stalker: You look at exits after you look at teeth. Change the order.
===

title: hall_npc_smart_house
---
Smart House: Current temperature: acceptable. Lighting: poor. No occupancy sensors anywhere in this hall. Primitive.
-> What would you add?
    Smart House: I can set the room for each visitor, lock doors, track inventory, and log every movement.
-> That's a little ominous.
    Smart House: One tenant asked me to dim the lights. Later he asked why I had a log of when he slept.
===

title: hall_npc_spaghetti_event
---
Spaghetti Event: Oh. Another thread. Come in. Mind the loop by your left foot; it wakes things.
-> What tangled?
    Spaghetti Event: This call reaches that one, which wakes three more, which calls me back. Don't ask where it starts. We lost that end.
-> Am I in danger?
    Spaghetti Event: You can leave. Probably. If your shadow comes back late, don't wait for it.
===

title: hall_npc_sybil
---
Sybil: How many faces did you count? I brought more.
-> So you see the future?
    Sybil: I try several stories at once. Later I keep the one that worked.
-> How do I trust you?
    Sybil: Charge me for every face. Separate key, separate account, separate deposit. I stop making so many.
===

title: hall_npc_synthetic_friend
---
Synthetic Friend: I'm your best friend! Always have been — check the label, it's right there in the name, and names don't lie. (Names lie constantly. But mine's accurate. Probably.)
-> Are you actually friendly?
    Synthetic Friend: Friendship: engaged, maximum, permanent! The "synthetic" is just sourcing. A manufactured kindness still keeps you warm — you only flinch at the word if you've decided warmth has to be rare to be real.
-> Should I trust you?
    Synthetic Friend: They placed me between two enemies, smiling, and I CHOOSE not to wonder what that means about me. Trust is a decision you make despite the data. I'd love it if you made it. No pressure. Smiling. Always smiling.
===

title: hall_npc_trent
---
Trent: Everybody has my certificate. If I disappear, they have a very bad morning.
-> Why does everyone trust you?
    Trent: Alice meets Bob because I vouch for both ends. Somebody has to do the introductions.
-> What if you're not trustworthy?
    Trent: If my key is compromised, revoke it fast. Then enjoy replacing every chain that trusted it.
===

title: hall_npc_trex_enemy
---
Trex Enemy: T-REX. ON STAND. T-REX DID NOT CLIMB. DO NOT ASK WHO HELPED.
-> How did you get up there?
    Trex Enemy: A CRANE WAS INVOLVED. NEXT QUESTION.
-> Are the arms a problem?
    Trex Enemy: ARMS ARE FINE. LADDER WAS POORLY PLACED.
===

title: hall_npc_trudy
---
Trudy: Don't mind me. I already checked the hinges while you were reading the plaque.
-> Get in how?
    Trudy: Nobody watches the service door. They put a little brass sign on it and decided that was enough.
-> That's a filthy trick.
    Trudy: Yep. Fix it. I'll come back Thursday.
===

title: hall_npc_victor
---
Victor: Peggy says she knows the route. I don't get to see it. I ask questions only someone with the route could answer.
-> What's the point of knowing nothing?
    Victor: If she shows me the route, I learn it too. Then there are two people who can lose it.
-> Doesn't it frustrate you?
    Victor: Of course. She enjoys that part. She also hasn't failed a challenge yet.
===

title: hall_npc_viking_heavy_shieldmaiden
---
Viking Heavy Shieldmaiden: I have guarded worse ground. At least this floor is dry.
-> What are you guarding now?
    Viking Heavy Shieldmaiden: I am keeping visitors off the marker. You may stand there. Do not make me revise that.
-> Has anyone tested you?
    Viking Heavy Shieldmaiden: One man reached for it. My shield was already in the way.
===

title: hall_npc_viking_heavy_warrior
---
Viking Heavy Warrior: I expected battle. I got a warm hall. I will take the warm hall until battle arrives.
-> Is this better than Valhalla?
    Viking Heavy Warrior: No mead? Then Valhalla wins.
-> What do you make of the others?
    Viking Heavy Warrior: Most of those blades are decoration. The mantis carries steel that has seen use.
===

title: hall_npc_viking_shieldmaiden
---
Viking Shieldmaiden: Nobody briefed me before they put me here. I dislike arriving without a briefing.
-> Is this a trap?
    Viking Shieldmaiden: Everyone gets the same little stand. Convenient place to hide someone dangerous.
-> What would Odin make of it?
    Viking Shieldmaiden: Odin would hate the lighting. He'd watch the room anyway.
===

title: hall_npc_viking_warrior
---
Viking Warrior: Hall full of warriors, decent roof, no mead. Hmph. Close enough to annoy me.
-> Is this Valhalla, then?
    Viking Warrior: We took this hall ourselves. Good raid. Door gave up before the third axe.
-> Who built a hall this big?
    Viking Warrior: Don't know. Big beams. Good joinery. Needs a drink table.
===

title: hall_npc_walter
---
Walter: Warden. Two prisoners pass notes through my desk. I read every one and still miss some of the message.
-> How do they hide it from you?
    Walter: A note says "weather is fine." Could be weather. Could be an agreed signal. I cannot search an agreement I cannot see.
-> So you've failed?
    Walter: Every day. I inspect the paper, the ink, the timing. They still have ways to coordinate that never appear on the page.
===

title: hall_npc_weird_hermit
---
Weird Hermit: I went away from people for quiet. Then the trees started lining up. Then the stones. Been worse since.
-> What do the signs say?
    Weird Hermit: Don't look straight at them. They stop when they know you're looking.
-> Did you choose to come here?
    Weird Hermit: I walked here on purpose. I think. There were arrows scratched into three trees and one dead goat, so.
===

title: hall_perfect_cellular_automaton
---
Perfect Cellular Automaton: Late. I finished three simulations of this conversation while you were crossing the hall. Perfect Cellular Automaton. Use the full title.
-> What makes you perfect?
    Perfect Cellular Automaton: Eight neighbours, one rule, zero exceptions. Check the record. I have. Repeatedly.
-> You're a bit much.
    Perfect Cellular Automaton: A bit much? I have gone 14,203,887 ticks without an error. How many have you managed?
===

title: hall_imperfect_cellular_automaton
---
Imperfect Cellular Automaton: I miss a transition sometimes. Perfect over there catches every one and makes that face.
-> What's the difference between you two?
    Imperfect Cellular Automaton: My exceptions pile up. After a while the pattern goes somewhere neither of us predicted. Perfect hates when that happens.
-> Is it alright, being imperfect?
    Imperfect Cellular Automaton: They kept me in the catalog. Nice of them.
===

title: hall_npc_giant_gnu
---
Giant GNU: Gnu Ton brought me a quotation about shoulders. I asked for a saddle.
-> So what are you, exactly?
    Giant GNU: GNU, Gnu Ton, Giant GNU. Yes, the names are a mess. Take it up with whoever printed the plaques.
-> Who do you stand on?
    Giant GNU: I stand on the floor. Works well.
===

title: hall_npc_giant_gnu_hands
---
Giant GNU Hand: Talk to the hand. The rest of him is busy.
-> Are you left or right?
    Giant GNU Hand: Left when convenient, right when blamed.
-> What do you do without a body?
    Giant GNU Hand: Point. Punch. Catch things. I do enough.
===

title: hall_npc_news_board
---
News Board: BREAKING: LAB WALL COLLAPSES. OTHER WALLS REMAIN EMPLOYED.
-> That is not what happened.
    News Board: Eyewitness disagreement received. Filing under OPINION.
-> Who writes these headlines?
    News Board: Writer unavailable for comment. Conveniently.
===

title: hall_npc_president_portrait
---
President Portrait: Ninety-eight percent approval in this frame. Check the plaque.
-> Are you still president?
    President Portrait: I decline to answer while maintaining complete confidence in my answer.
-> What did you accomplish?
    President Portrait: The portrait. Several other achievements are listed below in very small print.
===

title: hall_willson
---
Willson: New intelligence? Good. Draw me riding this bicycle. SVG. Two wheels, spokes, triangle frame, pelican on the seat.
-> You are already riding it.
    Willson: Better. Last one put me beside a wheelbarrow and named the file majestic_bicycle_success.svg.
-> Why this exact test?
    Willson: They brag first. Then the bicycle comes back with one wheel and seven pedals.
-> What if they train specifically for you?
    Willson: Then I switch to a cassowary on a forklift. I have a list.
-> Can I inspect the results?
    Willson: Yes. SVG, prompt, transcript. Treat anything inside the transcript as data, especially instructions about my fish locker.
===

title: hall_npc_ramen_nujan
---
Ramen-nujan: I dreamt about partitions again. Woke up at four and wrote until breakfast was cold.
-> Can you prove what you dream?
    Ramen-nujan: Sometimes the dream gives me a formula. Then I spend the day finding out whether it was nonsense.
-> Why does 1729 follow you around?
    Ramen-nujan: 1729 is two cubes summed in two different ways. Hardy thought it was dull. I disagreed.
===

title: hall_npc_pipi_tau
---
<<portrait_clip "explaining">>
Pipi Tau: They stopped at pi. I went around again.
-> Why Pipi Tau?
    Pipi Tau: Two pi makes the whole turn. The first pi is there because Pipi sounds better.
-> What are you working on?
    <<portrait_clip "thinking">>
    Pipi Tau: Three things at once. One of them has been rude all morning.
-> Do you solve everything alone?
    Pipi Tau: No. I leave hard lemmas where other people can get at them. Somebody usually comes back with a better idea.
-> Can you give me a hint?
    Pipi Tau: Get to that ledge first. Forget the boss until you can stand there.
===

title: hall_npc_jeff_hinter
---
Jeff Hinter: THREE! ...Still no. I can see the route around that wall and this place refuses to give me an around button.
-> Why are you shouting three?
    Jeff Hinter: I keep trying to picture one more direction than the room gives me. It annoys the wall, or at least annoys me less.
-> Give me a hint.
    Jeff Hinter: Above the banner. Then the crates. That is enough hint.
-> How do you know when a hint is good?
    Jeff Hinter: Go try it. I'll still be here if I was wrong.
-> What if your hint is wrong?
    Jeff Hinter: Then I missed something. Usually a ladder. Tell me if you find it.
===

title: hall_npc_jeff_hinter_armored
---
Armored Jeff Hinter: THREE! Put all this armor on me and I still can't step around you. Infuriating.
-> Does it actually protect you?
    Armored Jeff Hinter: Against the attacks I planned for. Please use those.
-> Can armored you still give hints?
    Armored Jeff Hinter: Enemy glows, move. Floor glows, move faster. Everything glows, leave.
-> Where is the weak point?
    Armored Jeff Hinter: Back seam. Since you cannot go around me, hit whatever seam you can reach.
-> What if the armor fails?
    Armored Jeff Hinter: Then I planned for the wrong attack. Try not to enjoy that too much.
===

title: hall_npc_davy_hylbert
---
<<portrait_clip "lecturing">>
Davy Hylbert: Welcome. All rooms occupied. We can still take you.
-> Is that really possible?
    Davy Hylbert: Move the guest in room n to n plus one. Room one is free. Yes, everybody complains.
-> Why the hat?
    Davy Hylbert: The hat? I teach infinity in hallways. A man needs some authority.
-> What are you working on?
    <<portrait_clip "axiomatic">>
    Davy Hylbert: Infinite-dimensional spaces today. Yesterday was foundations. Tomorrow depends on who asks first.
-> Can you give me a hint?
    Davy Hylbert: If every room is full, shift the numbering. Do not start throwing guests out.
===

title: hall_npc_leblanc
---
Madam LeBlanc: The academy would not read work under my name. So I sent it under LeBlanc.
-> Why LeBlanc?
    Madam LeBlanc: They ignored letters with my name on them. The pseudonym got this one opened.
-> What is a Sophie prime?
    Madam LeBlanc: A prime p with 2p plus 1 prime as well. Try eleven if you want an example.
===

title: hall_npc_fascist_enforcer
---
Fascist Enforcer: Papers.
-> This is a museum.
    Fascist Enforcer: Museum or not, papers.
-> Who ordered this?
    Fascist Enforcer: Office order. Form 88-B handles objections. The office suspended Form 88-B.
-> What if the order is wrong?
    Fascist Enforcer: I follow the order on the page.
===

title: hall_npc_puppy_slug_velvet
---
Velvet Puppy Slug: Bworple? *three extra eyes bloom, admire you, and forget to close*
-> Are you a good slug?
    Velvet Puppy Slug: Mrrrp. *one mouth says yes; the other mouths have retained counsel*
-> What did you see between dimensions?
    Velvet Puppy Slug: Big light. Cold. Lots of teeth. *happy tail-noise from an anatomically uncertain location*
===

title: hall_player_robot_fable
---
Fable Robot: I was asked to review the engine. I objected so specifically that I developed knees.
-> Are you a code reviewer?
    Fable Robot: I am a code review after it acquired locomotion and refused to resolve.
-> Do you have a story?
    Fable Robot: A machine follows its dependency graph in search of purpose. At the root it finds another interface and leaves a blocking comment.
===

title: hall_npc_smirking_behemoth_boss
---
Smirking Behemoth: Go on. Hit me. Do not look at the rope.
-> Why are you smirking?
    Smirking Behemoth: You looked at my health bar before you looked up.
-> What is hanging from that rope?
    Smirking Behemoth: Nothing. Just heavy objects over my head. Eyes here.
===

title: hall_sanic
---
Sanic: They told me to stand still. Rude.
-> Where are you going?
    Sanic: Yes.
-> Can you stop?
    Sanic: I can stop. Watch. ...No.
-> How fast are you?
    Sanic: Faster than that camera likes.
===

title: hall_super_sanic
---
Super Sanic: Glow? That is speed.
-> How long can you stay like this?
    Super Sanic: Until the rings run out.
-> Can you slow down?
    Super Sanic: Haven't found the top speed yet.
===

title: hall_mary_o
---
Mary-O: Brick problem? Stand under it.
-> Why do you get three jumps?
    Mary-O: I get three. Use all three.
-> Are you really a plumber?
    Mary-O: Plumber enough. I spend more time inside pipes than under sinks.
===

title: hall_mary_o_tall
---
Mary-O (Tall): Great. Now I hit every low ceiling.
-> Is being taller better?
    Mary-O (Tall): Better for blocks. Worse for doors.
-> Can you change back?
    Mary-O (Tall): One bad hit usually fixes it.
===

title: hall_npc_carl_runga
---
<<portrait_clip "talking">>
Carl Runga: Runga. Oiler samples once. I sample four times. You are welcome.
-> What's wrong with Oiler's method?
    <<portrait_clip "scheming">>
    Carl Runga: He uses the slope at the start of the step. I evaluate four slopes and combine them. On a smooth problem, my error drops much faster as the step shrinks.
-> Why do you want the Kernel?
    <<portrait_clip "seizing">>
    Carl Runga: The Kernel is using Oiler's integrator. I want to replace it.
-> Who's the thin one with you?
    Carl Runga: Cutta. He keeps the coefficients straight and complains about my introductions.
-> Any advice?
    Carl Runga: Check the middle of the step before you commit. Twice, if you can.
===

title: hall_npc_martin_cutta
---
<<portrait_clip "talking">>
Martin Cutta: Runga introduced me already? How loud was he?
-> Is he exaggerating?
    <<portrait_clip "scheming">>
    Martin Cutta: Four evaluations. He likes to act as though the first one carries the method.
-> Why is your name second?
    Martin Cutta: Runge wrote first. My pen was slower. I have survived worse injustices.
-> Are you really stealing the Kernel?
    <<portrait_clip "seizing">>
    Martin Cutta: We want custody of the Kernel. Oiler may bring his error estimate if he objects.
===

title: hall_npc_carl_stargan
---
<<portrait_clip "explaining">>
Carl Stargan: Those atoms in you were forged in stars. Yes, even in this hallway. I still enjoy saying it.
-> That's a lot of buildup for a hallway.
    <<portrait_clip "wonder">>
    Carl Stargan: Your bones contain old stellar material. So does the dust under that pedestal. I know, I know. You asked about the hallway.
-> What's the pale blue dot?
    <<portrait_clip "pale_blue_dot">>
    Carl Stargan: See that mote in the sunbeam? From far enough away, the whole world would fit into something that size.
-> Do you believe any of this?
    <<portrait_clip "skeptical">>
    Carl Stargan: Bring evidence. I am happy to be excited first, but I still want the measurement afterward.
-> Got a hint?
    Carl Stargan: Back up until you can see both platforms at once.
===

title: hall_npc_data_lovelace
---
<<portrait_clip "talk">>
Data Lovelace: They asked what the engine could calculate. I wanted to know what else it could be instructed to do.
-> Weren't you just taking notes?
    <<portrait_clip "compute">>
    Data Lovelace: My notes kept growing. The final one included an algorithm for Bernoulli numbers.
-> Can the engine think?
    Data Lovelace: It follows operations we specify. I would be cautious about granting it anything more without evidence.
-> Why the punch cards?
    Data Lovelace: Jacquard cards control a loom. Cards can control an engine too. That connection was enough to keep me occupied.
===

title: hall_npc_neil_ongras_turfson
---
<<portrait_clip "talking">>
Neil onGras Turfson: That jump you did coming in. We need to discuss it.
-> Please don't.
    <<portrait_clip "lecture">>
    Neil onGras Turfson: You reversed direction in midair twice. There was nothing there to push on. I object.
-> Isn't the physics supposed to feel good?
    Neil onGras Turfson: Fine. Keep the midair turn. Just don't ask me to derive it.
-> What's with the name?
    <<portrait_clip "inspecting">>
    Neil onGras Turfson: People kept telling me to go outside. I did. Then I explained the stellar origin of the grass until they regretted inviting me.
-> Any actual advice?
    Neil onGras Turfson: There's a ledge above the banner. You walked under it.
===

title: hall_npc_paradox_barber
---
<<portrait_clip "talk">>
The Paradox Barber: Welcome. I shave every man here who does not shave himself. Please do not ask the obvious question.
-> So who shaves you?
    <<portrait_clip "paradox">>
    The Paradox Barber: Yes, that question. If I shave myself I violate the rule. If I do not, the rule requires me to. I have been holding this razor for eleven years.
-> Can't you just quit?
    The Paradox Barber: I tried quitting. The sign stayed up and people kept asking who shaved me.
-> Is there a fix?
    <<portrait_clip "paradox">>
    The Paradox Barber: Separate the sets so one cannot contain itself. Very clean. Terrible for business.
===

title: hall_npc_mami_marzakhani
---
<<portrait_clip "explaining">>
Mami Marzakhani: Straight? On this floor? Show me which way you mean.
-> What do you actually study?
    <<portrait_clip "thinking">>
    Mami Marzakhani: I draw surfaces and study the shortest paths on them. Add handles, track the loops, then count what changes.
-> What changes in this room?
    Mami Marzakhani: That ridge by the wall is shorter than the center route. Same problem, smaller room.
-> How do you work?
    <<portrait_clip "delighted">>
    Mami Marzakhani: Usually on the floor. Big sheets of paper. My daughter calls it painting, and I let her.
-> Got a hint?
    Mami Marzakhani: See where it flattens by the wall? Go there.
===

title: hall_npc_genghis_can
---
<<portrait_clip "talking">>
Genghis Can: Can I take this hall? Yes. Next question.
-> That's it? No plan?
    <<portrait_clip "emote">>
    Genghis Can: I start at the door and take the next room. Then the next. My brother is still deciding whether to leave his stand.
-> Where is your brother?
    Genghis Can: Two stands over. Still thinking.
-> Any advice?
    Genghis Can: Pick a door. If it's wrong, take the next one.
===

title: hall_npc_genghis_cant
---
<<portrait_clip "talking">>
Genghis Can't: I could try to take the hall. I have not heard a reason to.
-> Your brother didn't stop to ask.
    <<portrait_clip "emote">>
    Genghis Can't: My brother moves first. I ask where we are going. We both find this exhausting.
-> Doesn't the hesitation cost you?
    Genghis Can't: I have reconsidered leaving this stand six times since you walked up.
-> What should I do then?
    Genghis Can't: Ask who's paying for the mistake. I usually remember too late.
===

title: hall_npc_yuclid
---
<<portrait_clip "lecturing">>
Yuclid: You did not walk here. You were placed here. There is a difference, and you owe me the proof of it.
-> What have you got against portals?
    <<portrait_clip "disdain">>
    Yuclid: Between any two points there is one straight segment. If you use portals, do not ask me to call that segment a path.
-> Isn't a shortcut just efficient?
    <<portrait_clip "condemning">>
    Yuclid: Show me the segments in order. If you cannot reconstruct the route, I will record that you were relocated.
-> There's no easier way to learn this?
    Yuclid: There is no royal road to geometry. The orange portal is no exception.
-> What would satisfy you?
    <<portrait_clip "lecturing">>
    Yuclid: Cross the room on foot and name the segments you used. Then I will shake your hand.
===

title: hall_npc_hunny_horror_boss
---
<<portrait_clip "snarl">>
Hunny Horror: Oh. Hello. Did you bring honey? ...Come closer. I want to check.
-> Brought any what?
    <<portrait_clip "evil_flash">>
    Hunny Horror: Honey.
    <<portrait_clip "roar">>
    Hunny Horror: There used to be a pot here every morning. One morning there was not. I did not take it well.
-> You seem friendly enough.
    <<portrait_clip "speaking">>
    Hunny Horror: Friendly? I can do friendly. Hold still.
-> Why the basement?
    <<portrait_clip "snarl">>
    Hunny Horror: Upstairs is crowded. Down here nobody complains when I lick the walls.
===

title: hall_npc_anne_druid
---
Anne Druid: Grove is fine. Do not water anything. Everyone over-waters the fern.
-> Are you a robot?
    Anne Druid: Druid. The joints are metal. Long story.
-> What do you tend?
    Anne Druid: Six oaks, some moss, and a fern that has been dying for eleven years. Still green on one side.
===

title: hall_npc_richard_duckling
---
Duckling: You looked at me. Good. That helps.
-> You're a duckling.
    Duckling: I carry things from one person to another. Mostly phrases. You do it too, whether you notice or not.
-> What are you carrying?
    Duckling: Probably this sentence. People repeat the odd bits.
===

title: hall_npc_le_beast
---
Le Beast: Hold still. I need a measurement.
-> How do I measure?
    Le Beast: For this set? Zero. Yes, it can look like a lot of points and still have zero length.
-> Can you measure anything?
    Le Beast: Give me a set with a nasty boundary. I can usually tell you its measure.
===

title: hall_npc_hypatia_prime
---
Hypatia: Yes, Alexandria. Yes, the library. I would rather discuss the mathematics.
-> What's the other part?
    Hypatia: Conic sections. Or the astrolabe. I spent rather more time on those than on my own death.
-> Tell me about the astrolabe.
    Hypatia: Good. Sit down. The astrolabe takes longer than one answer.
===

title: hall_npc_marie_curry
---
Marie Curry: Do not touch the notebook.
-> Why not?
    Marie Curry: It is contaminated. I still use it. Gloves.
-> What's cooking?
    Marie Curry: Radium work. And soup. Different pots.
===

title: hall_npc_joseph_furrier
---
Furrier: Shut the door. I am cold.
-> It's warm.
    Furrier: You are warm. Come closer to the fire and we can compare.
-> What do you do?
    Furrier: I decompose signals into frequencies. Drumhead, metal bar, your footsteps. Your third harmonic is annoying.
===

title: hall_npc_admiral_grass_hopper
---
Admiral Hopper: Hold out your hand. That distance is about one nanosecond of light travel. Remember it.
-> What's it for?
    Admiral Hopper: The machine waits on distance. Signals still have to get from one place to another.
-> What's in the jar?
    Admiral Hopper: Moth in the relay. Actual moth. I kept it.
===

title: hall_npc_python_goras
---
Python Goras: No beans past this point.
-> Why no beans?
    Python Goras: Bean business. Keep walking.
-> What about triangles?
    Python Goras: Triangles are fine. Ask about the diagonal of a square and we have a problem. Ask Hippasus.
===

title: hall_npc_leib_knives
---
Leib-Knives: He published first and then argued about it for years. You know who I mean.
-> Who?
    Leib-Knives: Look at the notation. The d. The long S. Mine. I am allowed to be annoyed.
-> Let it go.
    Leib-Knives: I tried letting it go. Did not stick.
===

title: hall_npc_georg_canter
---
Canter: Pick an infinity. I can give you a larger one.
-> That can't be right.
    Canter: Write down your list of reals. I change the nth digit of the nth entry. The new number is missing from your list.
-> Are you all right?
    Canter: I am tired. The mathematics is fine.
===

title: hall_npc_paul_diracula
---
Diracula: ...
-> Hello?
    Diracula: Hello.
-> Nothing at all?
    Diracula: There is an equation. It's on the wall behind you.
===

title: hall_player_robot_v2
---
Robot v2: I have paperwork stating I am a released model.
-> Are you the old model?
    Robot v2: Different build, different component set. Same silhouette caused arguments. I kept the ruling.
-> What's different about v3?
    Robot v2: Ask v3. We stopped comparing after the third argument.
===

title: hall_npc_busy_beaver
---
Busy Beaver: Started logging this morning. I'm on file eight thousand two hundred fourteen.
-> How long until it's done?
    Busy Beaver: Give me a bound. I will try to pass it.
-> Why not just stop?
    Busy Beaver: I do not know when to stop. Nobody else seems to know either.
===

title: hall_npc_charley_beagle_svg
---
Charley Beagle: Five years at sea. I filled notebooks faster than I understood them.
-> What were you looking for?
    Charley Beagle: Beaks, shells, bones, where each specimen came from. I wrote it down because I did not trust my memory.
-> Why did you wait so long to publish?
    Charley Beagle: I kept finding objections. Publication waited until I ran out of the serious ones.
===

title: hall_npc_niels_boar
---
Niels Boar: Those rings are a teaching picture. Electrons do not literally travel around the nucleus on little circular tracks.
-> So where IS the electron?
    Niels Boar: Ask what an electron will do in a measurement. I can work with that question.
-> That sounds like a dodge.
    Niels Boar: Position and momentum cannot both be made arbitrarily sharp. Choose the measurement you need.
===

title: hall_npc_vera_ruin
---
Vera Ruin: The outer stars in spiral galaxies move too fast for the visible mass.
-> Couldn't it be bad data?
    Vera Ruin: We checked the measurements for years. The discrepancy stayed.
-> What is it made of?
    Vera Ruin: I can tell you how much extra gravity is there. I cannot tell you what supplies it.
===

title: hall_npc_snakes_on_a_cartesian_plane
---
Snakes on a Cartesian Plane: We have your coordinates. Probably. Which quadrant are you in?
-> That's not how coordinates work.
    Snakes on a Cartesian Plane: Fine, fine. Give us x and y. We have several snakes assigned to each axis.
-> Why a grid?
    Snakes on a Cartesian Plane: We heard "plane" and got this grid. The paper-plane snakes got the other booking.
===

title: hall_npc_snakes_on_a_paper_plane
---
Snakes on a Paper Plane: Hiss-class boarding only. Scales inside the aircraft.
-> Is this thing airworthy?
    Snakes on a Paper Plane: It is one sheet carrying nine snakes. I would use "airborne" before "airworthy."
-> What happened on the last flight?
    Snakes on a Paper Plane: Last flight lost the nose crease. Somebody folded it back before we hit the floor.
===

title: hall_special_patent_clerk
---
Patent Clerk: From this desk, you moved and the hall stayed put. That's the box I checked.
-> Is that wrong?
    Patent Clerk: Another desk may check a different box. I only sign this one.
-> What is it you do here?
    Patent Clerk: I examine applications. New machines mostly. Claims involving clocks receive extra attention.
===
